{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S4 — Best-effort OpenAI-compatible endpoint: honor REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL, retire the loud refusal\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/llm/runner.py:718` (`_pai_check_config`) raises on any `base_url`/`api_key`, while\n`docs/llm-framework.md:126-133,226` documents both as working and shows an LMStudio/Ollama recipe, and\n`src/rebar/llm/config.py:502-503,611-612` already parses them. The documentation is false today. The refusal was\na deliberate placeholder: commit `75e598a41` describes it as \"a loud guard that REFUSES base_url/api_key rather\nthan silently dropping them (a capability gap vs langgraph, surfaced not hidden)\". This story fills the\nplaceholder it was created for.\n\n## Approach\n\nRegister an `openai` builder in the provider factory [rebar:7468-25e5-ae4f-43d1] that constructs\n`OpenAIChatModel` with `OpenAIProvider(base_url=cfg.base_url, api_key=…)`, gated behind the opt-in\n`pydantic-ai-slim[openai]` extra with a clear missing-extra error. Crucially, `base_url` is provider\n**configuration**, not provider **selection**: the provider still comes from the model string /\n`REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER`, exactly as `docs/llm-framework.md:132` already documents\n(`REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER=openai REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL=…`). Capability handling comes free from S2\n[rebar:f184-a5f1-f181-4700] — an opaque endpoint resolves to the conservative record, so structured output takes\nthe prompted path without any per-call boolean.\n\n### WHEN the `openai` builder is registered — resolved, not left to the implementer\n\nS1 (`7468`, closed) made `run()` resolution three-way: a provider in `ProviderSession._builders` is **eagerly**\nbuilt via `infer_model(provider_factory=...)`; a provider pydantic-ai recognizes but rebar does not build is\nleft as a **lazy model STRING**; a name neither resolves raises `LLMConfigError`. Today `_builders` holds only\n`anthropic`, so `openai` takes the lazy path.\n\nThat is load-bearing. The `openai` SDK is **not installed** (verified: `find_spec(\"openai\")` is None; rebar's\n`[agents]` extra deliberately omits it, and `pydantic_ai.providers.openai` raises `ImportError` at import).\nS1's implementation already hit this: calling `infer_model` unconditionally broke the parameterized\n`openai:gpt-4o` case in `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`, which stubs `_pai_structured` precisely so no\nreal provider is ever constructed.\n\n**Decision: the `openai` builder is registered ONLY when `cfg.base_url` is set.** A bare `openai:gpt-4o` with\nno `base_url` keeps taking S1's lazy-string path, byte-for-byte as today, so no currently-passing test changes\nbehavior and no optional SDK becomes mandatory.\n\nThis does **not** make `base_url` a provider selector, which the plan rightly forbids. The provider is still\nchosen by the model string / `REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER`; `base_url` only decides whether rebar constructs that\nprovider *itself* (to inject the endpoint) or defers to pydantic-ai. The documented recipe at\n`docs/llm-framework.md:131-133` sets `REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER=openai` **explicitly alongside**\n`REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL`, so this matches rebar's own published contract exactly.\n\nRejected alternatives: registering unconditionally (breaks the existing test above and makes the `openai`\nextra a hard requirement), and adding `pydantic-ai-slim[openai]` to the dev/test env (a change to rebar's\ndependency posture that deserves its own decision, not a side effect of this story).\n\n**Size budget:** `providers.py` is 225 LOC against the **300-LOC cap that is an attested acceptance criterion\nof closed story S1**. The builder must fit, or move to a leaf of its own — it must not silently breach a signed\ncriterion.\n\n`_pai_check_config` stops refusing and instead validates: an absolute-URL check on `base_url`, and an\n`api_key`-without-`base_url` error (ambiguous, since the direct OpenAI path reads `OPENAI_API_KEY`). For a\nno-auth local server an explicit placeholder key is sent so construction succeeds; a hosted endpoint answers\nwith its own 401.\n\nThis story also **documents the accidental capability** found during design: a non-loopback `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`\nalready routes rebar through an Anthropic-wire gateway, because `anthropic_model.py:60`\n(`_local_proxy_bypass_base_url`) only overrides loopback hosts and the SDK reads the env var. It works today by\naccident; this story makes it deliberate and tested.\n\n**Alternative rejected:** branching on `cfg.base_url` before provider inference (PR #121's shape). That makes\n`base_url` silently override an explicit `REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER`, contradicting rebar's own documented\nrecipe, and adds a fourth implicit provider selector alongside the model string, the provider env var, and\n`ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/providers.py` — the `openai` builder.\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — `_pai_check_config` (**`:718`**; the plan originally cited `:653`, stale\n  after S1/S2 moved code) becomes validation.\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py` — composition semantics for `base_url` + `model_provider`.\n- `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py` — replace `test_unsupported_config_is_a_loud_error`.\n- `tests/unit/test_openai_compatible_provider.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\nContract tier: the defect class is a consumer (the runner) reading configuration the wrong way, so the test must\nrun through real config resolution rather than calling the builder directly.\n\n- happy path: `REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER=openai` + `REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1` yields an\n  `OpenAIChatModel` whose provider carries that exact base URL and the configured api_key.\n- contrast case (the PR #121 regression this exists to prevent): `REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic` +\n  `REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL=…` still resolves the **anthropic** provider — base_url must not hijack selection.\n- failure paths: `api_key` without `base_url` raises `LLMConfigError`; a non-absolute `base_url` raises naming\n  the variable; a missing `openai` extra raises naming the install command.\n- edge: no api_key + a local base_url constructs successfully with the placeholder key.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the exact recipe printed at `docs/llm-framework.md:131-133` runs end-to-end against a local\n      OpenAI-compatible server (or a stub server in-test) and returns a valid structured verdict\n- [ ] a test asserts `REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic` + `REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL` resolves the anthropic provider\n- [ ] `_pai_check_config` no longer raises for a valid `base_url`, and its three validation errors each have a test\n- [ ] a test pins the `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` non-loopback gateway behavior so it can no longer change by accident\n- [ ] a REGRESSION GUARD test asserts a bare `openai:gpt-4o` with NO `base_url` still takes S1's lazy\n      model-STRING path and constructs no provider — proving the `openai` SDK stays optional and that the\n      existing parameterized `openai:gpt-4o` case in `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py` is unaffected\n- [ ] `providers.py` stays under the 300 LOC fixed by S1's attested criterion (or the builder lives in its own\n      leaf module), and `grep -rn 'openai' src/rebar/llm/runner.py` shows no provider-name branch added there\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the FULL gating suite (`make test`, not just `tests/unit`) pass\n- [ ] each acceptance criterion above is discharged by a NAMED test, listed in a ticket comment before close —\n      S2 closed late because half of one criterion had no test despite an 18-test oracle"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785376357360930001,"uuid":"9ca663f9-7031-47a9-9f9c-2f0998fa2146"}